self-check failed: acceptance criteria not met or not reported: "A new unit test in athena-core builds the closing trailers for a verification with verifier_invocation None and a failed check named fmt. It asserts the Athena-Verifier value is exactly `none (check fmt failed)` and does not contain the verifier model name. Run `cargo test -p athena-core`."; "A test asserts that when verifier_invocation is Some, the trailer is still `<verifier-model> pass` for a pass verdict and `<verifier-model> fail` for a fail verdict. Run `cargo test -p athena-core`."; redacted report: {"summary":"A job rejected by a check before any verifier ran now gets `Athena-Verifier: none (check <name> failed)`, naming the first failed check. If no check failed either, the value is `none (no verifier ran)`. When a verifier ran, the trailer is unchanged: `<model> pass` or `<model> fail`.

The root cause was in run.rs. The closing commit chose the trailer from the final verdict alone, so a check-rejected job still named the verifier model. I moved the choice into a small `verifier_trailer` function that branches on whether `verifier_invocation` is set. I added three unit tests for it, covering the `fmt` case, the no-failed-check case, and pass/fail with a verifier.

